      "id": 1,
      "text": "McBride’s roots trace back to 1874 when Alexander B. McBride built a sawmill that became the village’s first industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://discovermontcalmpodcast.com/mcbride-michigan-located-within-day-township/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s post office, named “McBrides,” opened on March 26, 1878, with McBride himself as the first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McBride%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "McBride once served as a key shipping hub for the Pere Marquette Railroad, moving lumber and farm goods across Michigan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://discovermontcalmpodcast.com/mcbride-michigan-located-within-day-township/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic McBride Cemetery, part of Day Township, houses graves of early pioneers and a Grand Army of the Republic post.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://discovermontcalmpodcast.com/mcbride-michigan-located-within-day-township/"
    },
    {
